        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-Sébastien Bérubé\n- Organizations: New Jersey Devils, Albany Devils\n- Places: Newark, Prudential Center\n- Events: 2008 NHL Entry Draft, 2007–08 New Jersey Devils relocation\n- Topics: professional ice hockey, American Hockey League\n\nFacts:\n- Beginning with the 2007–08 season, the New Jersey Devils relocated to Newark and began playing their home games at the Prudential Center.\n- In the 2008 NHL Entry Draft, the New Jersey Devils selected Jean-Sébastien Bérubé in the 7th round with the 205th overall pick.\n- Jean-Sébastien Bérubé was born on July 20, 1990.\n- Jean-Sébastien Bérubé is a Canadian professional ice hockey player.\n- Jean-Sébastien Bérubé was playing for the Albany Devils in the American Hockey League at the time of this text.",
